## Workflow ownership

| Activity | Owner |
|---|---|
| Patient eligibility | Hospital clinical lead |
| Check-in question configuration | Aescia (with clinical sign-off) |
| Urgency rule definition | Clinician-led, Aescia-supported |
| Worklist review | Hospital clinical team |
| Escalation decision | Hospital clinician |
| Escalation execution | Hospital clinical pathway |
| Data governance | Joint — site and Aescia |
| Evaluation reporting | Aescia (with site review) |
| Adverse event reporting | Hospital lead, with Aescia notification |

Clinical responsibility for all patient management decisions rests with the treating clinical team at all times.

---

## Governance touchpoints

| Stage | Governance activity |
|---|---|
| Scoping | Governance requirements scoped and checklist produced |
| Configuration | Clinical sign-off on rule set and patient materials |
| Pre-launch | Privacy impact assessment, data governance agreement, ethics (if required) |
| During pilot | Adverse event monitoring, operational safety review |
| Close | Evaluation report, site governance debrief |

---

## Integration options

**No integration (default for initial pilots)**
Aescia operates as a standalone system. Patient enrolment is managed directly. Worklist access is via the Aescia platform. No EMR read/write is required.

**Optional lightweight integration**
Where available, integration options may include: automated enrolment from discharge data, worklist display within existing clinical tools, or discharge summary flagging. These are scoped as enhancements after the core pilot workflow is validated.

